                                    <!-- Embedded Thumbnail Image - Placeholder -->
                                    <img src="https://placehold.co/400x200/4C4C4C/FFFFFF?text=Start+Point+Assessment" 
                                        alt="Placeholder Image: Assessment Diagram"
                                        class="w-32 h-auto cursor-pointer rounded-lg shadow-md hover:shadow-xl transition-shadow duration-200"
                                        onclick="openImageModal(this.src)">
                                    <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-2 italic">Click image to expand view. **(Always replace with a relevant screenshot/diagram.)**</p>
                                </div>
                            </div>

                            <!-- ACCORDION 2: Best Practice: High-Leverage vs. Low-Cost -->
                            <div class="goodblock-card primary p-4">
                                <button class="accordion-header flex justify-between w-full text-left items-center" data-target="step4-content-2">
                                    <div>
                                        <h4 class="font-bold text-lg mb-0" style="color: var(--brand-primary);">Best Practice: Maximize Leverage</h4>
                                    </div>
                                    <span class="accordion-icon transition-transform duration-300 text-gray-400">▼</span>
                            </button>
                                <div id="step4-content-2" class="accordion-content hidden pt-4 mt-4 border-t border-gray-100">
                                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-700">Prioritize actions that, once completed, will save you significant time in the future. Example: Learning a keyboard shortcut is a high-leverage action because the 10 minutes spent learning it saves you hours over a lifetime.</p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <p class="mt-6 text-lg font-semibold" style="color: var(--brand-secondary);">Once you've identified the starting point, we move to the three execution steps.</p>`,
            },
            // STEP 5: Topic 2.2: The Three Configuration Fields - Generic
            { 
                title: "Topic 2.2: The Three Execution Steps", 
                body: `<p class="mb-4 text-gray-700">Execution is defined across three key steps: **Step 1 (The Trigger)**, **Step 2 (The Script)**, and **Step 3 (The Habit)**.</p>
                       <p class="text-lg font-semibold" style="color: var(--brand-secondary);">We will now walk through the configuration of these three steps sequentially.</p>`,
            },
            // STEP 6: Step 1: Configure Field 1 (The Foundation) - Generic
            { 
                title: "Step 1: Define the Trigger (The Foundation)", 
                body: `<p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">The **Trigger** is the external event or internal feeling that initiates the desired new action. **You must define the trigger before you can replace the old bad habit with a new good one.**</p>
                        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
                            <!-- A. Time Trigger -->
                            <div class="p-3 border-l-4 rounded bg-gray-50" style="border-color: var(--brand-secondary);">
